.TH SDL_copyp 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_copyp \- A macro to copy memory between objects, with basic type checking.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_copyp(dst, src)                                                                 \(rs
.BI "    { SDL_COMPILE_TIME_ASSERT(SDL_copyp, sizeof (*(dst)) == sizeof (*(src))); }             \(rs
.BI "    SDL_memcpy((dst), (src), sizeof(*(src)))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR SDL_memcpy
and
.BR SDL_memmove
do not care where you copy memory to and from, which can lead to bugs\[char46] This macro aims to avoid most of those bugs by making sure that the source and destination are both pointers to objects that are the same size\[char46] It does not check that the objects are the same _type_, just that the copy will not overflow either object\[char46]
.PP
The size check happens at compile time, and the compiler will throw an error if the objects are different sizes\[char46]
.PP
Generally this is intended to copy a single object, not an array\[char46]
.PP
This macro looks like it double-evaluates its parameters, but the extras them are in
.BR sizeof
sections, which generate no code nor side-effects\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I dst
a pointer to the destination object\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I src
a pointer to the source object\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

